{"assets":["/statement-assets/422cc9cd43f2d096866f34fdef764720c6def313b415ba4b94ff1efe4794af4f.png","/statement-assets/a26ef1106e2ac462ba88f627a53e4d4ffe847a4e6b171656d763e261acf9894e.png","/statement-assets/02e7280eb708f0a27d7f3ceee936f21c9e3b70f3b5ffb12bea92eec1bd2fb67e.png","/statement-assets/aa92d8241ac13da5b7dd894ddf2aebd82107d922e68a75f3ffe692daf204a45f.png","/statement-assets/22a717ef7d2bd5b78a946e34b029c544dbf8db2794fff876f76246b3c2c457bf.png","/statement-assets/ee052c5b4748d424f701f90d252f0ba577bf7c48884c18a2109d08195418c761.png","/statement-assets/79246d419b0ffa371d0386b8ba81b191362a6c6e24bc992bc9e466ae69db17b6.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"164","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Polycarpus and Tasks"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarpus has many tasks. Each task is characterized by three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":". Three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(li, ri, ti)"},{"kind":"text","text":" mean that to perform task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":", one needs to choose an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(li ≤ si; si + ti - 1 ≤ ri)"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the task will be carried out continuously for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" units of time, starting at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" and up to time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si + ti - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive. In other words, a task is performed for a continuous period of time lasting "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":", should be started no earlier than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":", and completed no later than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarpus's tasks have a surprising property: for any task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j, k"},{"kind":"text","text":" (with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j < k"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"lj < lk"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"rj < rk"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's suppose there is an ordered set of tasks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":", containing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|A|"},{"kind":"text","text":" tasks. We'll assume that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj = (lj, rj, tj)"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ j ≤ |A|)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also, we'll assume that the tasks are ordered by increasing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"lj"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the increase in number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the following recursive function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f"},{"kind":"text","text":", whose argument is an ordered set of tasks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the result is an integer. The function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(A)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is defined by the greedy algorithm, which is described below in a pseudo-language of programming."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 1. "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/422cc9cd43f2d096866f34fdef764720c6def313b415ba4b94ff1efe4794af4f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ans = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 2. We consider all tasks in the order of increasing of their numbers in the set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":". Lets define the current task counter "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 3. Consider the next task: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i = i + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i > |A|"},{"kind":"text","text":" fulfilled, then go to the 8 step. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 4. If you can get the task done starting at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" = max"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(ans + 1, li)"},{"kind":"text","text":", then do the task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" = max("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ans + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":"), "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ans = si + ti - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a26ef1106e2ac462ba88f627a53e4d4ffe847a4e6b171656d763e261acf9894e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Go to the next task (step 3). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 5. Otherwise, find such task "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/02e7280eb708f0a27d7f3ceee936f21c9e3b70f3b5ffb12bea92eec1bd2fb67e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", that first, task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be done at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" = max"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/aa92d8241ac13da5b7dd894ddf2aebd82107d922e68a75f3ffe692daf204a45f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and secondly, the value of "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/22a717ef7d2bd5b78a946e34b029c544dbf8db2794fff876f76246b3c2c457bf.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is positive and takes the maximum value among all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk"},{"kind":"text","text":" that satisfy the first condition. If you can choose multiple tasks as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk"},{"kind":"text","text":", choose the one with the maximum number in set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 6. If you managed to choose task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ee052c5b4748d424f701f90d252f0ba577bf7c48884c18a2109d08195418c761.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/79246d419b0ffa371d0386b8ba81b191362a6c6e24bc992bc9e466ae69db17b6.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Go to the next task (step 3). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 7. If you didn't manage to choose task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk"},{"kind":"text","text":", then skip task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":". Go to the next task (step 3). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Step 8. Return "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ans"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a result of executing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(A)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarpus got entangled in all these formulas and definitions, so he asked you to simulate the execution of the function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f"},{"kind":"text","text":", calculate the value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(A)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of tasks in set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the tasks. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains three space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ li ≤ ri ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ti ≤ ri - li + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the description of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th task."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that for any tasks "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j, k"},{"kind":"text","text":" (considering that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j < k"},{"kind":"text","text":") the following is true: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"lj < lk"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"rj < rk"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" print a single integer — the result of processing task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th iteration of the cycle (step 3) in function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(A)"},{"kind":"text","text":". In the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line print:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" 0 — if you managed to add task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" on step 4. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" -1 — if you didn't manage to add or replace task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" (step 7). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"resi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ resi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — if you managed to replace the task (step 6): "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"resi"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals the task number (in set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":"), that should be chosen as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk"},{"kind":"text","text":" and replaced by task "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 8 5\n2 9 3\n3 10 3\n8 11 4\n11 12 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0 1 0 -1 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"13\n1 8 5\n2 9 4\n3 10 1\n4 11 3\n8 12 5\n9 13 5\n10 14 5\n11 15 1\n12 16 1\n13 17 1\n14 18 3\n15 19 3\n16 20 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0 0 2 -1 -1 0 0 0 0 7 0 12 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"164E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/164/problem/E"}